  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A gas undergoes a complete thermodynamic cycle. The internal energy of the gas before the cycle is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{1}\"></span> and after the cycle it is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{2}\"></span>. What is true about <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{2}\\,?\"></span></p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">The relationship between <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{1}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{2}\"></span> can only be determined if we know the initial volume, pressure, and temperature of the gas.</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{1} &gt; E_{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{1} &lt; E_{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{1} = E_{2}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
